# "{T}, Sacrifice five artifacts: Take an extra turn after this one." The Sieve is one of the five artifacts it sacrifices. An
# activated ability's costs are paid together (CR 602.2b, 601.2h), so the {T} is paid while the Sieve is still a permanent: it
# becomes tapped on the battlefield (CR 701.26a) and is sacrificed tapped, which its last-known information says (CR 608.2h).
# `LeftBattlefield` reads the history in order: had the tap been recorded after the sacrifice, the Sieve would not show as
# tapped. The four Moxen it sacrifices with it were tapped for mana on turn 1 and untapped in Bot1's turn-3 untap step, so they
# leave untapped. The extra turn follows (CR 500.7).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Time Sieve
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Island
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Time Sieve.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Time Sieve.Activate
Bot1.Choose(Tap Time Sieve)
Bot1.Choose(Time Sieve; Mox Sapphire; Mox Jet; Mox Ruby; Mox Pearl)
? LeftBattlefield = Time Sieve (tapped); Mox Sapphire; Mox Jet; Mox Ruby; Mox Pearl
[T4 Bot1.Main1]

[Expect]
Turn = 4
ActivePlayer = Bot1
LeftBattlefield = Time Sieve (tapped); Mox Sapphire; Mox Jet; Mox Ruby; Mox Pearl
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 5
